Package: yogabook-camera
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pipewire, wireplumber
Recommends: snapshot
Description: Lenovo Yoga Book YB1-X90F cameras for PipeWire
 yb-camerad publishes the AtomISP front (OV2740) and rear (OV8858) sensors as
 two PipeWire cameras with their location, rotates the frames to follow the
 screen and opens /dev/video0 only while an application streams. A WirePlumber
 rule hides the raw AtomISP node.
 .
 GNOME Camera is started without GL and graphics offload (a Mesa GL-thread
 race and a GTK 4.18 offload bug crash it on this hardware); the package
 diverts /usr/bin/snapshot to a wrapper that does this.
